      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A mortgage is a legal agreement and financial instrument in which a lender (typically a bank or financial institution)  provides a borrower with funds to \npurchase real estate, most commonly a home. The property itself serves as collateral (security) for the loan. If the borrower fails to repay the borrowed \namount plus interest according to the agreed terms, the lender has the right to take possession of the property through a process known as foreclosure.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A mortgage is a legal agreement and financial instrument in which a lender (typically a bank or financial institution)  provides a borrower with funds to \npurchase real estate, most commonly a home. The property itself serves as collateral (security) for the loan. If the borrower fails to repay the borrowed \namount plus interest according to the agreed terms, the lender has the right to take possession of the property through a process known as foreclosure.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
